thread:
maria: Seeing constant 429s on the sample app onboarding flow when prefetch + concurrency are on. Only starts after STS token rotate. Anyone seen this?

sam: which SDK + version? and your rate limiter settings?

maria: js-sdk v0.26.2, prefetch window=30, concurrency=8. STS creds TTL=60s. After a refresh we get a burst of 429s for ~20-40s. Happens reproducibly on heavy startup.

chen: can you paste the response headers/logs around the refresh? curious about x-rate-limit-remaining / reset and any session ids.

maria: sure — here's the trimmed client flow:

```js
// pseudo-code from sampleapp prefetcher
async function prefetchBatch() {
  for (let i=0; i<prefetchWindow; i++) {
    if (inflight >= concurrency) break;
    inflight++
    client.generate(prompt).finally(() => inflight--);
  }
}

// auth refresh hook
auth.on('refresh', async (newToken) => {
  client.setToken(newToken);
  // we were not pausing prefetch here
});
```

rate-bot: example 429 headers we recorded: x-ratelimit-limit: 100, x-ratelimit-remaining: 0, x-ratelimit-reset: 1672531200, x-client-session: sess_abc123

sam: my gut: token refresh causes a client-side churn (new session id / connection) + prefetch immediately ramps, so server sees N new clients or burst of new requests and triggers quota policing. add jitter + short pause after refresh to let pooling/stickiness settle.

maria: added 200-500ms jitter on refresh + pause prefetch for 5s after refresh — reduced frequency but still some 429s under heavier load.

chen: this could be related to session keying on the server that uses token fingerprint. I'll grep the routing codepath for session attribution. @devex can we add a short note in the onboarding guide recommending 'pause prefetch after token refresh' and an example?

devex: yes — will add a small recipe to the sampleapp docs: "Graceful auth rotation: pause background prefetch + reuse HTTP agent". I'll create a PR and link it here (#4598).

sam: also recommend keeping the same keep-alive HTTP agent so downstream sees a stable connection id. for node: new https.Agent({ keepAlive: true }) and reuse across token swaps.

maria: good tip, thanks. creating a minimal repro now (small script that refreshes STS every 45s + prefetch window 40). will post results and headers when ready.

chen: thanks — if you can attach the repro I can try to run it against staging and trace session attribution.

maria: will do, pushing link in ~10m. :thumbsup:
